<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crusade of Varna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1443">1443</a>–<a href="/years/1444">1444</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a> was a campaign of 1443–1444 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, Wallachia and others, led by King Władysław III and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a>. After the successful 'Long Campaign' of 1443 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-szeged">Peace of Szeged</a>, the crusaders renewed the war and were crushed at Varna in November 1444, where Władysław was killed, ending hopes of driving the Ottomans from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crusade-of-varna.jpg" alt="Crusade of Varna" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Varna_1444.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
